# Research and sources

Follow `docs/source-policy.md`.

- Prefer official and contemporary evidence appropriate to the claim.
- Map every important claim to an exact source location and distinguish
  publication date, event date, and public-knowledge time.
- Attribute expectations; label cautious interpretation; preserve unresolved
  disagreement.
- Never guess, silently combine incompatible accounts, or use a citation for
  more than it supports.
- Isolate cutoff-safe facts from later sources and flag spoiler-bearing sources.
- Quote briefly only when exact wording adds historical value.

Use the `historical-f1-research` and `source-verification` skills for substantial
work. The globs anticipate the provisional architecture; apply this rule
wherever historical research or claims are handled.
